{"type": "sena", "_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "lesson_name", "content": "Peter Visits Vanessa at Work"}, {"type": "unit_name", "content": "A  Must-Try"}, {"type": "position", "content": 3}, {"type": "origin", "content": "stub"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 7}, {"type": "level", "content": "B1.2"}], "type": "metadata"}, {"contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}], "type": "achievment_test"}, {"contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": "Use expressions about relationships and feelings in a range of social and work contexts. "}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": "Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about common technology."}, {"type": "secondary_2", "content": "Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about common technology."}, {"type": "secondary_3", "content": "Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about common technology."}, {"type": "secondary_4", "content": "Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about common technology."}, {"type": "secondary_5", "content": "Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about common technology."}, {"type": "secondary_6", "content": "Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about common technology."}, {"type": "secondary_7", "content": "Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about common technology."}, {"type": "secondary_8", "content": "Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about common technology."}], "type": "objectives"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Talking about Wishes and Imaginary Situations  "}, {"type": "describer", "content": "You use <span class =\"italic\">\u201cI wish\u2026\u201d</span> to talk about things you do not have or do, or you cannot have or do."}, {"type": "text", "content": "The verb <span class =\"italic\">wish</span> introduces an idea. After <span class =\"italic\">wish</span>, you use a verb in the past tense."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I wish I knew ... <br/>I wish I had ... <br/>I wish you were ... "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Structure: <br/>Wish + Simple Past tense"}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":5,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">Example</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">Meaning</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class =\\\"italic\\\">I wish it came with rice instead of potatoes.</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"I want it to come with rice, but it comes with potatoes.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class =\\\"italic\\\">I wish I had a good recipe for stir-fry.  </span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"I want to have a good recipe for stir-fry, but I don't.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class =\\\"italic\\\">I wish we were going to Ned's.</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"I want to go to Ned's, but I'm not going there.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class =\\\"italic\\\">I wish we served lobster!</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"I would like us to serve lobster, but we don't.\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border\"}"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Discussing How to Deal with Problems"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "One way to discuss how to deal with problems is to say what you would do if you were in someone else's situation. This is a polite way of communicating if you use the modals <span class =\"italic\">would</span> or <span class =\"italic\">could</span>.<br/><br/><span class =\"italic\">I would ... <br/>I wouldn't ... <br/>You could ... "}, {"type": "text", "content": "These are examples of Peter and Vanessa giving suggestions about how to deal with problems. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "<span class=\"strong\">Vanessa</span>:  I was disappointed with the meal.  I'll have to talk to the chef.<br/><span class=\"strong\">Peter</span>: I wouldn't worry about it, Vanessa. Maybe he just had a bad day."}, {"type": "example", "content": "<span class=\"strong\">Peter</span>: I'm a bit stressed, because Tracy is coming over.<br/><span class=\"strong\">Vanessa</span>: I would practice the recipe first.  "}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "must-try"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "something you have to taste"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Here's a must-try: baked chicken in mushroom sauce. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn7le07ob03aud01"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "These are words you use when you talk about food."}], "type": "target_word_describer"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "stir-fry"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a way of cooking by mixing ingredients like meat and vegetables in a large pan"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example:  I usually get the beef and broccoli stir-fry."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn7le07ob03aud02"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "drumsticks"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "part of the chicken you eat"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: You should order the baked chicken drumsticks.  "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn7le07ob03aud03"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "oven-roasted"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "describes food that has been cooked in the oven, usually over a long period of time"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: It comes with oven-roasted greek potatoes. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn7le07ob03aud04"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "cod"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a type of white fish"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Today, I think I'll have the lemon baked cod. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn7le07ob03aud05"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "frustrated"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "feeling frustration; not getting what you want"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I'm a bit frustrated, because all my recipes are boring."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn7le07ob03aud06"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "engenn7le07ob03re1img01.jpg"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Find a large piece of paper the size of a poster."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Draw a line dividing the paper in half, and then lines dividing it into 4 more sections to make a total of 8 sections (see example below). "}, {"type": "text", "content": "On the left side, write adjectives ending in <span class=\"italic\">-ed</span>, like <span class=\"italic\">frustrated</span>. Try to find different adjectives than the example."}, {"type": "text", "content": "On the right side, write adjectives ending in <span class=\"italic\">-ing</span>, like <span class=\"italic\">exciting</span>."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Ask 10 people questions starting with: <span class=\"italic\">\u201cWhen do you feel ...\u201d</span> or <span class=\"italic\">\u201cWhat do you find ...\u201d</span>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Write their answers in the correct category."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Share your poster with a partner or the class."}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":4,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"excited:\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"exciting:\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"frustrated:\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"frustrating:\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"tired:\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"tiring:\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"bored:\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"boring:\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\"\"}"}], "type": "takeaway_extension"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "I ask people about their feelings and reactions."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I write explanations for feelings and reactions."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I share the information."}], "type": "takeaway_assessment"}], "labs": [{"exercises": [{"questions": [], "img_path": "", "stimuli_ids": [0], "template_override": 1, "type": "WLC", "_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": "I can talk about feelings and reactions. "}, {"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": " I can talk about wishes and imaginary situations."}, {"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": " I can discuss how to deal with problems. "}, {"type": "Free Header Item", "content": " When do you feel frustrated? Tired? Excited?  Why?"}, {"type": "Free Header Item", "content": " What do you find frustrating? Tiring? Exciting?  Why?"}], "type": "instructions"}, {"con